  "name": "Gandrang pakarena (Gowa court dance drumming)",
  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Music of the pakarena, the women's dance of the former Gowa court of the Makassar in South Sulawesi. Two drummers on the gandrang, a double-headed barrel drum struck with a stick and the hand (the Malay gendang card and the generic membrane-drum card stand in), play fast, forceful patterns with the puik-puik shawm (the serunai card stands in) and a gong, while the dancers move with slow, restrained grace; that contrast is the form's hallmark.",
